{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XyVsV2K5GvJXYjaHv96c3T","type":"tool_result","content":"13:If the default highlighting doesn't fit your needs, you can define a custom highlighter. The easiest way to do this is to extend the :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` class which applies a style to any text matching a list of regular expressions.\n18:    from rich.highlighter import RegexHighlighter\n21:    class EmailHighlighter(RegexHighlighter):\n25:        highlights = [r\"(?P<email>[\\w-]+@([\\w-]+\\.)+[\\w-]+)\"]\n43:While :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` is quite powerful, you can also extend its base class :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter` to implement a custom scheme for highlighting. It contains a single method :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter.highlight` which is passed the :class:`~rich.text.Text` to highlight."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c75d1021-0f0b-4d4e-bbb6-05b27484d4bb","uuid":"ede86c6a-c612-4586-9685-31b160565d03","timestamp":"2026-10-25T12:47:56.435Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"13:If the default highlighting doesn't fit your needs, you can define a custom highlighter. The easiest way to do this is to extend the :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` class which applies a style to any text matching a list of regular expressions.\n18:    from rich.highlighter import RegexHighlighter\n21:    class EmailHighlighter(RegexHighlighter):\n25:        highlights = [r\"(?P<email>[\\w-]+@([\\w-]+\\.)+[\\w-]+)\"]\n43:While :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` is quite powerful, you can also extend its base class :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter` to implement a custom scheme for highlighting. It contains a single method :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter.highlight` which is passed the :class:`~rich.text.Text` to highlight.","numLines":5,"totalLines":5},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XyVsV2K5GvJXYjaHv96c3T","permi